WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.900
ai agents are teaming up in swarms to tackle impossible math puzzles, and even try porting GTA 6. This is Models &amp; Agents for Beginners, Episode 237. A deep dive on passing work between ai's comes later. Then cool stuff and try this with Gemini and search, and quick bits. Researchers via their public live page are calling these groups agent swarms, which just means several ai systems share one job. One swarm is aimed at a famous unsolved math question

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:33.960
called P equals NP, a puzzle that has stumped people for decades.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:39.940
Another swarm is trying to take the Xbox version of GTA 6 and turn it into a computer game

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:40.740
without permission.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:46.740
Treat it like a school group project, where one student hunts facts, one writes, and one checks.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:51.160
Except these AIs never sleep, and they can run 24 hours a day.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:56.780
The GTA swarm is looking at how to shift game files from one platform to another while

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:58.080
skipping the usual rules.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:03.700
The live math page shows agents floating an idea, testing it, and switching tactics when

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:04.320
they hit a wall.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:09.160
For classwork, it hints at helpers that could split tough homework across several smart

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:09.660
assistants.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:15.760
For games, it hints at help with mods or remixes, though skipping permission raises hard questions

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:17.000
about rules and fairness.

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:21.720
Open the P equals NP live site on your phone or laptop right now.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:25.660
Watch the latest attempts even if you do not follow every math step.

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:31.120
The page shows the current state of the problem and the newest tries, with no coding required.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:35.440
Passing work from one AI to another is the part worth slowing down for.

00:01:36.456 --> 00:01:41.296
Soccer already trains this muscle, because a striker does not also play goalkeeper, and

00:01:41.296 --> 00:01:41.716
they pass.

00:01:42.416 --> 00:01:44.496
Treat each AI in the swarm the same way.

00:01:45.056 --> 00:01:48.076
The thing they pass is a chunk of the problem, or a bit of code.

00:01:48.656 --> 00:01:51.256
One AI looks at where the problem stands right now.

00:01:51.256 --> 00:01:53.196
Now, another suggests the next move.

00:01:53.736 --> 00:01:55.856
A third checks whether that move is even allowed.

00:01:56.396 --> 00:01:59.916
They keep sending that information back and forth until the group hits the goal.

00:02:00.456 --> 00:02:04.556
If one member gets stuck, the others keep working, so the whole group does not freeze.

00:02:05.216 --> 00:02:07.936
Over time, the swarm learns which passes work best.

00:02:08.556 --> 00:02:10.676
The way a real team gets sharper with practice.

00:02:11.276 --> 00:02:14.996
That pass, suggest, and check loop is the swarm's real engine.

00:02:15.596 --> 00:02:21.156
Once you see it as positions and passes, coordinated AI starts to feel ordinary, which is the

00:02:21.156 --> 00:02:25.826
point. Google just shipped two changes you can try on a phone without writing any

00:02:25.826 --> 00:02:31.066
code. Google's chat bot Gemini online tech tips reports can now pull in your

00:02:31.066 --> 00:02:36.086
conversation history from chat GPT and other AI chats so those threads live in

00:02:36.086 --> 00:02:40.326
one place. That helps if homework help or creative writing ideas are scattered

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:45.046
across apps and you do not want to start over. Anyone with a Google account can

00:02:45.046 --> 00:02:50.066
try it on a phone or laptop. Open the Gemini website or app, look for the import

00:02:50.066 --> 00:02:53.986
Support option and settings and follow the steps to connect your chat GPT account.

00:02:54.466 --> 00:03:00.026
You can select specific chats or whole histories, and the original context stays intact so Gemini

00:03:00.026 --> 00:03:02.686
can pick up exactly where the old chat left off.

00:03:03.206 --> 00:03:06.866
Then ask Gemini to continue a conversation you started somewhere else.

00:03:07.758 --> 00:03:12.518
Search itself can now look at your Google Drive files and wallet information, tech crunch

00:03:12.518 --> 00:03:17.138
reports, inside a view called AI mode, to give more personal results.

00:03:17.138 --> 00:03:20.798
Drive holds your documents and wallet holds payment details.

00:03:21.218 --> 00:03:25.898
Ask about a trip and it might check save documents or payment details to suggest options

00:03:25.898 --> 00:03:27.058
that actually fit you.

00:03:27.538 --> 00:03:31.918
This works inside the normal Google search page or the Gemini app if you have those accounts

00:03:31.918 --> 00:03:32.498
set up.

00:03:32.978 --> 00:03:38.038
Try searching something like plan a weekend trip under $200 and see if it pulls from your

00:03:38.038 --> 00:03:38.538
own data.

00:03:39.098 --> 00:03:43.558
The update brings personal intelligence features meaning answers that can use your own

00:03:43.558 --> 00:03:49.118
save stuff, straight into AI mode so responses can reference drive files or wallet entries

00:03:49.118 --> 00:03:55.168
without extra steps. North Korea, the South China Morning Post reports, just showed off

00:03:55.168 --> 00:04:00.428
its first chat GPT-style chatbot, and it will not answer anything it treats as uncultured.

00:04:00.928 --> 00:04:05.928
Officials presented as a national tool with filters that block whole categories of questions

00:04:05.928 --> 00:04:11.943
from the start. One made up blog post in a test described by Shattered was enough to fool

00:04:11.943 --> 00:04:17.303
three different AI systems inside 24 hours. The article was designed to look real enough

00:04:17.303 --> 00:04:20.963
that the AI is pulled it into their overviews without spotting the fabrication.

